#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vcheck — the course's pinned verifier wrapper (phase DV1b).

Design §7.1 ("the verifier part"), §14.2; spec §8.3, §11.1 rows 1, 2, 17, 22;
DELTAS Δ10–Δ14, Δ17, Δ41, Δ56–Δ59. The only way the course runs Dafny and
Verus: it always uses the pinned binaries, the pinned project or crate and
the pinned flags (all read by the dvl libraries from scripts/dvl/pins.toml),
and every job runs under the CLAUDE.md §Resources memory cap.

Usage:
  vcheck [--gate] [--json] [--symbol S | --module M --function F] [--seed N]
         [--isolate] <target> [-- <verifier args>]
      target: a unit directory (Dafny dfyconfig.toml dir, Verus crate dir), a
      project file, one .dfy/.rs file, or a *.dfy.specimen / *.rs.specimen
      (copied to scratch with its real extension).
  vcheck <ID> [d|v] / vcheck --module <ID> [--lang d|v]
      every verification unit of a module (the registry's `units`), learner
      loop settings unless --gate. Planned modules are refused.
  vcheck [--gate] [--json] <file.py> / vcheck <ID> py
      a learner Python file (harness/q/fvh_q/…, harness/r/fvh_r/…; with
      `<ID> py`, every file of the module's `harness` list): its holes,
      counted from the syntax tree by the frozen core (fvh.holes), then its
      acceptance tests (harness/tests/<t>/test_<stem>.py) through pytest,
      offline on the pinned uv lock, under the memory cap (dvl.python). The
      learner loop's verdict is the tests'; the gate passes only with zero
      holes and every test passing. Summary: `vcheck: <file> [python, <mode>]:
      <verdict> — <p> passed, <f> failed, <n> holes`. --ref on a twin
      (Solutions/harness/…) lays it over a scratch copy of harness/ and runs
      the same tests there; --test runs the tests alone; --shipped and
      --pin-counts include the file (role harness).
  vcheck --smt-log DIR [--symbol S] <Verus target>
      the learner loop (or the fast channel) with Verus's `--log smt` added:
      the SMT queries sent to Z3 are copied into DIR (new or empty, never in
      a reference tree) and listed as `smt log: <file> (<n> bytes)`; the run
      is the same capped run, with the same verdict and hole count (D53, R14:
      read the `:pattern` of each quantifier). Refused with the gate.
  vcheck --module <ID> <probe file>
      one probe (instructor/scratch/probe.dfy|rs) with the module's given
      layer chain and unit options.
  vcheck --brittleness [--solvers | --solver S] <target>
      re-verify under every pinned seed (Δ59); a verdict that differs between
      seeds fails; the resource-count spread is reported, never gating, and a
      symbol whose spread exceeds the pinned coefficient of variation (20%,
      pins.toml spread_flag_cv) is flagged, never gated (QPLAN §6 Q29).
      Dafny only (QPLAN §6 Q29, §17.5): --solvers re-verifies under every
      seed with each Z3 bundled with the pinned Dafny (pins.toml
      [dafny.solvers], the pinned 4.12.1 first), and --solver S under one of
      them; every row must verify for `stable`. Verus checks its Z3's version
      and has one solver (VERSIONS.md §1.2): both options are refused there.
  vcheck --solver <S> [--seed N] [--json] <Dafny target>
      the learner loop under another bundled Z3 (a measurement; QPLAN §6
      Q29). The done gate and the reference gate keep the pinned solver
      (Δ10): --solver with --gate or --ref (except --ref --brittleness) is
      refused. Solver pass-through after `--` stays refused.
  vcheck --ref --brittleness [--solvers | --solver S] <twin target>
      author-only: the same sweep on a reference twin, laid over its learner
      unit as --ref runs it (DV0-REPORT §8 item 37); locations only, never a
      symbol name or a message.
  vcheck --gate --lab-task <task form> [--json] <delivery>
      the lab gate (QPLAN §30 Q63; PLAN §4.3): the done gate on the
      delivery, plus the lever check against the task form it was made from
      (dvl.levers): a verification lever the task form does not ship (Dafny
      {:induction …}, {:fuel …}, {:vcs_split_on_every_assert}, assertion
      isolation, the nonlinear switch, resource, time and option attributes;
      Verus every verifier attribute but proof_note and triggers), a shipped
      one the delivery dropped, or a changed project file is a lab-lever-added,
      lab-lever-removed, lab-file-added or lab-project-changed finding, and
      the verdict is failed. Then, on a delivery still verified, vaudit's
      assumption rules (scripts/vaudit's audit, learner mode, the default
      trust allowlist; the user's decision D24): each finding is a lab-audit
      finding and the verdict is failed, so a delivery equal to a task form
      that ships `assume {:axiom}`, or a lever the lever check allows but the
      audit reports (a shipped `{:axiom}` lemma), does not pass. Two files of
      one language or two directories. The learner gate never applies it
      (learner files may carry the allowed levers). `specfreeze --lab` runs
      the lever check beside the freeze (its static half: no audit).
      On a Lab 2 card (a task form under bench/local/q/lab2/ or lab2pub/;
      the user's decision D27), after the lever check, the code check
      (dvl.labcode): the delivery keeps the task form's executable code token
      for token; it may add the target's specification, one witness call,
      definitions and lemmas, and on a public card (lab2pub/) proof
      annotations (invariants, assertions, proof blocks, lemma calls); any
      other difference is a lab-code-changed finding and the verdict is
      failed.
  vcheck --gate --lab-task <task form> --lab-code own [--json] <delivery>
      the lab gate without the code check, for an arm that writes its own
      code on a Lab 2 card (the vericoding arm V, QPLAN §25.5).
  vcheck --selftest
      the pinned toolchains pass their checks and verify tiny invented
      programs (one gate pass and one counted hole per language).
  vcheck --ref <target>
      author-only (CI=true or the author's linked worktree): the reference
      gate; prints the verdict and locations only, never a message. A twin
      runs in its learner unit; a directory of loose .dfy files that mirrors
      no learner path (the DV0 spikes) runs as one program with the pinned
      resource limit (and the standard library when a file imports Std). A
      unit twin is compared with its count pin: a stale pin fails.
  vcheck --ref --pin-counts <ID>
      author-only: run the reference gate on the twin of every unit of the
      module and write expected/<ID>.counts (Δ11): per unit, the twin's count
      and the learner-declared declarations with a contract that ran a task
      there; per file (schema 2, the Q8 decision), the shipped state of every
      exercise, check, exit and agent file in the learner loop: verdict,
      tool-counted holes and errors (run it on the files as shipped). Nothing
      is written unless every twin passes and every file gives a verdict.
  vcheck --shipped [--json] <ID> [d|v]
      every file of the module against its shipped-state pin in
      expected/<ID>.counts: the same verdict, holes and errors in the learner
      loop (a unit's files through one run of the unit, every other file on
      its own). Learner files only; scripts/ci.sh's verify jobs run it. It
      fails once a file is worked on: it checks the course as shipped.
  vcheck --bin <crate> [-- <arguments>]
      a Verus crate's command-line tool (the user's decision D16; QPLAN §30
      Q59; the capstone crate's `[[bin]]`, which scripts/gen_units.py
      generates): the crate's layer chain verified and exported, its library
      verified (the learner loop's normal mode: holes do not block it, as for
      --test; the done gate is --gate) and compiled, its one `[[bin]]` root
      compiled against it by the pinned `verus --crate-type=bin --compile`,
      then the binary run once with the arguments after `--`, in a scratch
      copy under the memory cap (dvl.verus.run_bin). Cargo is never used.
      Prints `vcheck: <crate> [verus, bin <name>]: built — N verified; ran
      `<name> <arguments>`: exit <n>`, then the program's standard output
      and (on stderr) its standard error. Exit 0 when it was built and
      exited 0; 1 otherwise (a build that failed prints why); 3 refused (no
      crate directory, not exactly one [[bin]] target, its root missing,
      reference material). The binary is deleted afterwards: run it again
      with new arguments.
  vcheck --test [--json] [--name N ...] <unit | crate | file | ID [d|v]>
      the compiled checks: Dafny {:test}/@Test methods (dafny test --target
      py) and Verus #[test] fns (verus --compile --test, then the binary),
      in a scratch copy under the memory cap (dvl.dafny.test,
      dvl.verus.test). One PASSED/FAILED line per test; exit 0 when every
      requested test (every test, without --name) ran and passed. Refused
      for reference targets, and for a target holding an enabled slot or an
      `after:` item whose first try is not recorded (H5).

Modes:
  learner loop (default)  Dafny --allow-warnings, Verus one --no-cheating run
                          (holes are counted, never fatal); exit 0 = verified.
  --gate                  the done gate: Dafny --allow-warnings false and a
                          positive verified count (Δ10, Δ11; the Δ3 lint is
                          vaudit's, Δ4: done = this gate AND vaudit); Verus
                          Δ12's one-run gate (success, whole crate, no VIR
                          error, verified >= the floor, no hole, lint at
                          zero). On a registry unit (the unit dir, a file of
                          its project or crate) the Δ11 count pin applies:
                          every symbol expected/<ID>.counts pins must have
                          run a task and the count must reach min_verified,
                          so a deleted lemma or hole fails; a unit with no
                          pin fails (count-pin-missing). Filters are refused.
  fast channel            --symbol S (Dafny Mod.Name, Verus f | m::f |
                          m::*::method) or --module M --function F (Verus,
                          Δ41); never a pass in the gate.

Verifier arguments after `--` pass through only when the library's refusal
list allows them (dvl.dafny.check_args: the learner loop may add the filters,
--isolate-assertions, --analyze-proofs, --extract-counterexample; the gate
none. dvl.verus.check_args: --expand-errors, --multiple-errors N, --triggers,
--triggers-mode M; the gate only the pinned rlimit and the seed option). The
legacy CLI, --allow-*, --no-verify, solver and Boogie pass-through, unpinned
limits and every other flag are refused (exit 3; Δ10, Δ13, Δ17, Δ18).

Output: one summary line, then one line per hole, diagnostic and finding as
`path:line:col: …` (paths relative to the repo root). A clean gate prints only
the summary line. The summary names the count in its own unit (Δ39):
`N verified` (Dafny tasks; Verus `verified`), `N assertions verified` under
Dafny --filter-position (W-D08), `N tasks passed` for a seeded Dafny run.
--json prints {lang, target, exit_code, verdict, stage, verified_count,
count_unit, holes, findings, diagnostics, per_symbol, raw_dir, cmd} (a list
for several units; count_unit: tasks | assertions | passed-tasks | verified).
With --measures (learner loop and fast channel only; DV5a integration, so
the default document the chapters quote is unchanged), --json adds two
measurements (R05.P3dv, R05.H1py): `resource_count`, the run's total solver resource count (Dafny:
the tasks' ResourceCount sum from the CSV log; Verus: the per-function
rlimit sum of the --time breakdown; null when the run left none, as a Verus
run that met a hole, and for Python), and `wall_s`, the wall-clock seconds
vcheck spent on the target. The gate's record carries neither (an instrument
document fvh hashes, Δ161).
A specimen whose prediction slots have no recorded first try is refused:
running it would print the answer (spec §3.8.4 H5). So is a specimen that
waits for a prediction: a card demo carrying `// after: <item id>` runs only
once that item's first try is recorded (vaudit and --test refuse it too).

Exit: 0 verified · 1 not verified (failed, inconclusive, killed(memory),
error) · 2 usage · 3 refused (unknown or planned module, missing file, a
refused option or target, a missing pinned toolchain).

Environment: DVL_SCRATCH, DVL_DAFNY_JOBS, DVL_VERUS_JOBS (dvl.common).

This file is also the tools' shared core: scripts/vaudit, scripts/specfreeze,
scripts/firsttry.py, scripts/pins.py and scripts/reference_lint.py load it
(load_core below) for the registry, target resolution, the author self-gate,
scratch shadow trees, calibration records and output formatting.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import contextlib
import dataclasses
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import statistics
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import tomllib
from dataclasses import dataclass
from datetime import date
from pathlib import Path

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True   # importing the shared modules leaves no scripts/__pycache__
SCRIPTS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
REPO = SCRIPTS.parent
if str(SCRIPTS) not in sys.path:
    sys.path.insert(0, str(SCRIPTS))

import course_items as ci  # noqa: E402  (the ONE item parser, Δ71)
import check_course_map as ccm  # noqa: E402  (registry, --resolve, module items)
import gen_units as gu  # noqa: E402  (layers, unit options)
from dvl import common  # noqa: E402
